```

When an `__init__.py` file is found, it creates a `Package` object that will attempt to collect tests from the package. The problem is that this causes `__init__.py` files from non-test packages to be collected and imported. The `__init__.py` should only be collected if it matches the `python_files` patterns (like `test___init__.py` or `__init___test.py`) or if it's explicitly part of the test path.

The `+ ["__init__.py"]` addition appears to be the culprit. Removing it would mean `__init__.py` files are only collected when explicitly specified on the command line or when they match the configured patterns. The Package class should handle discovering tests within packages, so `pytest_collect_file` shouldn't need to force collection of all `__init__.py` files. However, this raises a question about how tests defined directly in `__init__.py` would be discovered without this behavior.

